; Snowfield — 1st Snowfield terrain visual (habitat-tiers ruling, 2026-09-04 ->
; task-8-brief.md). Emits `snow` (project/data/terrain/snowfield.tres) — Husky habitat.
;
; Snowfield may border grass with no placement restriction (human ruling, spec OQ-E: the
; game is not restricted to real-world climate adjacency). Nothing in this scene or its
; `.tres` gates neighbours; that stays true after this task.
;
; Source: Ultimate Nature Pack, Quaternius, CC0 1.0 Universal — the pack's dedicated snow
; variant set (BirchTree_Snow_3.fbx, Bush_Snow_1.fbx), NEWLY imported this pass.
; License.txt re-checked at `source-content/assets/Ultimate Nature Pack - Jun 2019.../
; License.txt` per asset-import-pipeline.md's audit gate before import (same boilerplate
; CC0 1.0 text as every other use of this pack, e.g. Rock_1/BirchTree/Bush). Recorded in
; project/attribution/sources/quaternius_ultimate_nature_pack.tres.
;
; COMPOSITION: a pale snow-white slab (Color(0.92, 0.95, 0.98, 1)) carries 1x
; BirchTree_Snow_3 (a full-canopy tree, matched to the same ~2.5 tile-unit canopy-height
; target every other Forest/tree pick in this codebase uses) + 1x Bush_Snow_1 (matched to
; the same ~0.6 tile-unit ground-level shrub target Bush.tscn uses) + 2 pale-blue floor
; patches (same "no tileable snow ground texture exists in the audited packs" technique
; GrassCommonShort/PineTree already use, tinted for drifted-snow shading instead of
; moss/litter).
;
; SCALE: both raw meshes measured via a one-off SceneTree AABB probe (same procedure prior
; passes used). BirchTree_Snow_3 raw height 4.152866 -> scaled 0.602 (4.152866*0.602=2.500,
; the SAME 2.5 tile-unit canopy target CommonTree1/CommonTree2/PineTree/BirchTree all use —
; height stays a control variable, only the silhouette/season-dressing changes). Bush_Snow_1
; raw height 1.284088 -> scaled 0.4672 (1.284088*0.4672=0.600, the SAME 0.6 tile-unit target
; Bush.tscn's non-snow Bush_1 uses). FIRST-PASS PROPOSAL, no GDD number exists for either —
; FLAG FOR HUMAN SIGN-OFF, same open posture as every prior prop-scale call in this
; codebase.
;
; SINGLE VARIANT: ships with exactly one `model_scenes` entry — same posture as Meadow.tscn
; and Scrub.tscn; a multi-variant richness pass (e.g. a 2nd snow tree/bush pick, or the
; pack's PineTree_Snow_*/BirchTree_Dead_Snow_* siblings) is out of scope here.
;
; EVERYTHING GROUND-LEVEL NESTED UNDER ONE NODE NAMED "Slab" (OcclusionFader exemption
; convention, see CommonTree1.tscn's header); the tree and bush instances sit as plain
; siblings of Slab, same as every other terrain wrapper in this codebase.
